@startuml hyperv-uplink
!include _style.iuml
title Hyper-V hosts: LLDP leaves through the physical NIC

node "Windows host with Hyper-V" {
  component "WinLLDP" as w
  component "vEthernet (LAN)\nhost vNIC · IP · MAC aa:bb:..." as veth
  component "Hyper-V external switch" as vsw
  component "VM ports" as vm
  component "Ethernet\nphysical NIC · same MAC aa:bb:...\nno IP stack" as phy
}
node "Network switch" as sw

w --> phy : **sends** LLDP here\n(same MAC as the vEthernet)
phy --> sw : LLDPDU
w ..> veth : not here
veth --> vsw
vsw --> vm
vsw -[#B03A2E,dashed]-x phy : <color:#B03A2E>LLDP not forwarded\n<color:#B03A2E>to the uplink</color>
sw --> phy : neighbors' LLDPDUs
phy ..> w : captured, reported\nunder vEthernet (LAN)

note bottom of vsw
  Like any 802.1D bridge, the virtual switch does not forward
  the reserved address 01:80:c2:00:00:0e to its uplink.
end note
@enduml
